    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "1SA4:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "A man of Benjamin ran out of the army and came to Shiloh the same day, with his clothes torn and with dirt on his head."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA9:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now there was a man of Benjamin, whose name was Kish the son of Abiel, the son of Zeror, the son of Becorath, the son of Aphiah, the son of a Benjamite, a mighty man of valor."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA9:16",
        "textualBasisJa": "“Tomorrow about this time I will send you a man out of the land of Benjamin, and you shall anoint him to be prince over my people Israel. He will save my people out of the hand of the Philistines; for I have looked upon my people, because their cry has come to me.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA9:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "Saul answered, “Am I not a Benjamite, of the smallest of the tribes of Israel? And my family the least of all the families of the tribe of Benjamin? Why then do you speak to me like this?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA10:2",
        "textualBasisJa": "When you have departed from me today, then you will find two men by Rachel’s tomb, on the border of Benjamin at Zelzah. They will tell you, ‘The donkeys which you went to look for have been found; and behold, your father has stopped caring about the donkeys and is anxious for you, saying, “What shall I do for my son?”’"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA10:20",
        "textualBasisJa": "So Samuel brought all the tribes of Israel near, and the tribe of Benjamin was chosen."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA10:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "He brought the tribe of Benjamin near by their families and the family of the Matrites was chosen. Then Saul the son of Kish was chosen; but when they looked for him, he could not be found."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA13:2",
        "textualBasisJa": "Saul chose for himself three thousand men of Israel, of which two thousand were with Saul in Michmash and in the Mount of Bethel, and one thousand were with Jonathan in Gibeah of Benjamin. He sent the rest of the people to their own tents."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA13:15",
        "textualBasisJa": "Samuel arose, and went from Gilgal to Gibeah of Benjamin. Saul counted the people who were present with him, about six hundred men."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA13:16",
        "textualBasisJa": "Saul, and Jonathan his son, and the people who were present with them, stayed in Geba of Benjamin; but the Philistines encamped in Michmash."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA14:16",
        "textualBasisJa": "The watchmen of Saul in Gibeah of Benjamin looked; and behold, the multitude melted away and scattered."
      }
    ],
